  "why": "Goodbye, Lara, a 12 episode summer 2026 TV run airing 2026-07-05 to 2026-09-20 and still on air at labelling time. AniZip 18643 is the same run: SAME_AS ids to mal:58878 and anilist:177637 and the same episodeCount of 12. The Crunchyroll season GT00378059-GS00378060 is the same run: it maps SAME_AS onto all four members and its 10 episodes sit on the same Sundays as AniZip's first 10 (2026-07-05 through 2026-09-06) with the same titles, so it is the aired part of the cour, not a folded season (10 is fewer than 12). The JustWatch season 485469-511223 is the same run: it maps SAME_AS onto all four members and onto anizip:18643 and repeats nine of the same episode titles in order. The bare Crunchyroll series GT00378059 is a container with no dates, count or episodes of its own, and Kitsu records it as a PART_OF container for this run, so it holds the run. AniZip episodes 1 to 10 pair with the Crunchyroll episodes on matching broadcast days and identical titles (Mermaid Princess Lara through The Princess with a Blade), and with Kitsu's episodes 1 to 10, which carry exactly the same ten titles. Crunchyroll episodes 1 to 9 pair with the JustWatch ones on those same exact titles. JustWatch episode 10 is listed as Yaiba o Motta Princess, a romanised Japanese title rather than The Princess with a Blade, and JustWatch carries no dates, so that position is left unpaired; AniZip episode 11 (2026-09-13) has only the Japanese title and episode 12 none at all, and Kitsu's episodes 11 and 12 are untitled, so those positions are left alone too."
